exercise-A: 100.0 ns x 10.0 GB/s = 1000.0 bytes in flight = 15.6 blocks of 64 B; one block at a time would give 0.64 GB/s
exercise-B: 100.0 ns x 20.0 GB/s = 2000.0 bytes in flight = 31.2 blocks of 64 B; one block at a time would give 0.64 GB/s
exercise-C: 50.0 ns x 10.0 GB/s = 500.0 bytes in flight = 7.8 blocks of 64 B; one block at a time would give 1.28 GB/s
